Source: postgresql-@PGMAJOR@-adaptive-autovacuum
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: adaptive_autovacuum maintainers <noreply@github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-server-dev-@PGMAJOR@, jq
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/secp256k1-sha256/adaptive_autovacuum
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: postgresql-@PGMAJOR@-adaptive-autovacuum
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, postgresql-@PGMAJOR@, adaptive-autovacuum-setup (= ${source:Version})
Description: adaptive autovacuum controller extension for PostgreSQL @PGMAJOR@
 adaptive_autovacuum watches dead-tuple and freeze debt, worker saturation
 and host capacity, and adjusts PostgreSQL autovacuum settings within
 guardrails.
 .
 This package installs the shared library and the extension control and SQL
 scripts for PostgreSQL @PGMAJOR@. It does not restart PostgreSQL, change its
 configuration or create the extension; run "adaptive-autovacuum-setup install"
 (package adaptive-autovacuum-setup, installed as a dependency) for that.

Package: adaptive-autovacuum-setup
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, jq, bash (>= 4.2), util-linux
Description: setup, health-check and rollback helper for adaptive_autovacuum
 adaptive-autovacuum-setup discovers PostgreSQL clusters, appends
 adaptive_autovacuum to shared_preload_libraries while preserving other
 entries, restarts the selected service with consent and rollback, creates or
 updates the extension per database and runs the SQL health checks.
 .
 One helper serves every PostgreSQL major on the host; the
 postgresql-<major>-adaptive-autovacuum packages depend on it.
